{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun","id":1131291,"title":"The Etymology Thread [Just For Fun]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-19T08:47:07-07:00","id":1131291,"title":"The Etymology Thread [Just For Fun]","content":"Honestly, I can't say how many times I've looked at a new, cool thing which showed up in the CofD, be it a splat, an otherworld or an antagonist, and I thought for myself whether its name is made in actual language, a made up language, or a made up language inspired by real life language. While some of those words are easy to be found online, there's apparently a limit to Google's ability to find dictionaries in long dead languages, leaving me to forever wonder whether the word actually exist, or if it was made up. Most of the time, it doesn't matter whether the word is real or not, but sometimes it does- especially when you want to focus on a certain time or place in your setting, or make up new antagonists using the same language as canon used. This thread is for anyone who, like me, has words they have always wondered about where they came from and wants to get an answer.<br /> <br /> So, the words I want to ask about are-<br /> <br /> - Neglatu (it sounds like Sumerian, but I'm really not sure)<br /> -Noctuku (again, same thing as the Neglatu)<br /> - Acamoth and Gulmoth (is it made up? It sounds made up)<br /> <br /> so, those are mine- can anyone tell me from where those words come from? Anyone else has words they are wondering about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:21:21-07:00","id":1131339,"title":"","content":"A part of me thinks that the Noctuku is a Classic World of Darkness callback to the Nictuku, who were Nosferatu Vampires empowered by the Nosferatu Antediluvian (think Clan progenitor) to wipe out the rest of his clan as an attempt to apologize to Caine and remove his curse (which was supernatural ugliness). The renaming also feels similar to how the Malkovian Bloodline were a callback to the Malkavian Clan in the cWoD (replacing one of the vowels with an o that is).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:24:04-07:00","id":1131343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131339#post1131339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A part of me thinks that the Noctuku is a Classic World of Darkness callback to the Nictuku, who were Nosferatu Vampires empowered by the Nosferatu Antediluvian (think Clan progenitor) to wipe out the rest of his clan as an attempt to apologize to Caine and remove his curse (which was supernatural ugliness). The renaming also feels similar to how the Malkovian Bloodline were a callback to the Malkavian Clan in the cWoD (replacing one of the vowels with an o that is).</div> </div> </div> </div>oh, I'm aware for that- the question is if the word itself is based on a real word language, or was made up already in Masquerade?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:45:01-07:00","id":1131354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun#post1131291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Acamoth and Gulmoth (is it made up? It sounds made up)</div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf/Onyx Path have a long history of using words with modified spellings, so I tired messing with alternate spellings. 'Achamoth' is a term from gnosticism, though I'm not terribly clear on what it means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T14:00:33-07:00","id":1131432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131343#post1131343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh, I'm aware for that- the question is if the word itself is based on a real word language, or was made up already in Masquerade?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah I see. Pardon, I misinterpreted the meaning. ^^&quot; <br /> <br /> If &quot;Noctuku&quot; is based on the word &quot;Nictuku&quot; and not it's own word, the VtM lore says that &quot;Nictuku&quot; comes from a primeval word &quot;nek-duku&quot; meaning &quot;they who guide to death&quot;. However I can't find any examples of nekduku at all, so it might be good to take with a grain of salt. <br /> <br /> If it is it's own word, I don't know what it could be. I did find/make up abit of a funny meaning that still theoretically fits. &quot;Noct&quot; can mean &quot;Nightly/nocturnal&quot; and &quot;uku&quot; is apparently a Hawaiian word for &quot;Lice&quot;. Put it together and it comes to be &quot;Night Lice&quot;, which is actually kind of fitting for vampires (considering they're parasitic in terms of feeding and can only be up at night).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T15:03:05-07:00","id":1131462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131432#post1131432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If &quot;Noctuku&quot; is based on the word &quot;Nictuku&quot; and not it's own word, the VtM lore says that &quot;Nictuku&quot; comes from a primeval word &quot;nek-duku&quot; meaning &quot;they who guide to death&quot;. However I can't find any examples of nekduku at all, so it might be good to take with a grain of salt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's quite likely. It reminds me of 'Nephandi', which Ascension claimed might have been from 'Nif\u2019 ur `en Daah', or 'eaters of the weak' although Nefandi is a latin word, and Awakening uses it somewhat correctly as 'Nameless'.<br /> <br /> 'Course it's easy to see the mistake when you can just type the word into Wikipedia which wasn't around in 1998.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T22:55:27-07:00","id":1131629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131354#post1131354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> White Wolf/Onyx Path have a long history of using words with modified spellings, so I tired messing with alternate spellings. 'Achamoth' is a term from gnosticism, though I'm not terribly clear on what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's actually quit helpful! While the exact origin of the word isn't clear, the fact it comes from gnosticism means that if I want to make a new type of Abyssal Entities, I need to search for an appropriate gnostic term. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T22:58:11-07:00","id":1131631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131432#post1131432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah I see. Pardon, I misinterpreted the meaning. ^^&quot;<br /> <br /> If &quot;Noctuku&quot; is based on the word &quot;Nictuku&quot; and not it's own word, the VtM lore says that &quot;Nictuku&quot; comes from a primeval word &quot;nek-duku&quot; meaning &quot;they who guide to death&quot;. However I can't find any examples of nekduku at all, so it might be good to take with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> If it is it's own word, I don't know what it could be. I did find/make up abit of a funny meaning that still theoretically fits. &quot;Noct&quot; can mean &quot;Nightly/nocturnal&quot; and &quot;uku&quot; is apparently a Hawaiian word for &quot;Lice&quot;. Put it together and it comes to be &quot;Night Lice&quot;, which is actually kind of fitting for vampires (considering they're parasitic in terms of feeding and can only be up at night).</div> </div> </div> </div>amm.. so it sounds more and more like a made up word. I need to think about it, but I think I can handle it. Thank you for that! Now I only need to find the meaning behind Neglatu :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T23:15:21-07:00","id":1131635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131631#post1131631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I only need to find the meaning behind Neglatu :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Latin? The way of nothing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T23:42:39-07:00","id":1131640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131354#post1131354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> White Wolf/Onyx Path have a long history of using words with modified spellings, so I tired messing with alternate spellings. 'Achamoth' is a term from gnosticism, though I'm not terribly clear on what it means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Achamoth is challenging to explain. I think I have this correct though.<br /> <br /> Gnostics generally believe that their true God is Eternity, from which emanate five groups of beings known as Aeons, all of which are in Male/Female pairs. One of the female Aeons is Sophia, &quot;Wisdom.&quot; Sophia is sometimes portrayed dualistically, with Achamoth representing &quot;fallen wisdom.&quot; Note though that Achamoth wasn't evil, Fallen in this context is closer to the meaning of the Fallen World. Achamoth is fleshly and imperfect, yet still shields Souls from harm and begs the unfallen Sophia to send Christ to Earth to free humanity from Ialdaba\u014dth.<br /> <br /> If Acamoth is derived from Achamoth, the relation of the word to the Abyssal Beings is tenouous, but Gnosticism is probably your best bet for new Mage words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T07:44:00-07:00","id":1131704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1131291-the-etymology-thread-just-for-fun?p=1131635#post1131635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Latin? The way of nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>damn it google! you have failed me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}